{"n": 668, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "668.webp", "text": "1634 091\n\n34-24\n\nDESCRIPTION OF AND CHECKING ABS\nINDICATOR LAMP\n\nABS Indicator lamp lights up after\nswitching on ignition.\n\nIndicator lamp should go out when en-\ngine has started and ABS Is okay.\n\nProcedures are repated each time igni-\ntion Is switched off and on.\n\nCauses for faulty Indication (indicator\nlamp doesn't light up, doesn't go out\nor comes on while driving - even oc-\ncaslonally — can be found with help of\nBMW SERVICE TESTER and brake test\nstand (dynamometer).\n\nimportant!\nEach started step must be finished\ncompletely without a break!\n\nContro! unit will automatically switch\nto “normal braking” where there is elec-\ntric or electronic faults In ABS.\n\nThis means car can still be braked, but\nwithout control (wheel! could lock!).\nFaulty system will be indicated by a\ncontinuously lighted ABS indicator\nlamp In Instrument panel.\n\n325 IX (Cars with Four Wheel Drive):\n\nHf ABS Indicator lamp lights up while\ndriving, first measure resistance in ac-\nceleration sensor and electric wire (see\n34 52 000) betore testing ABS,\n\nCheck throttle valve adjustment (ste\n13 54 130) In case of Impaired comfort,\n€.g. hesitation or stalling of engine dur-\ning ABS regulation,\n\nABS of 325 IX cars may not be tested\non brake test stand (Test Steps 8,9\nand 10).\n\nGENERAL INFORMATION ON REPAIRS\nAND BRAKE SYSTEM\n\nBasically ABS does not require servic-\ning, however, pay attention to the fol-\n\nlowing points when working on cars\nwith ABS.\n\n@) Disconnect plug on electronic con-\ntrol unit (ignition switched off)\nwhen welding with electric welder.\n\nb) When painting, electronic control\nunit can be subjected to max. 95°C\n(203° F) briefly or max. 85° C (185° F)\nfor a longer period (about 2 hours).\n\nc) Battery terminals must be tightened\nperfectly on end poles of battery\nafter reinstallation of removed\nbattery.\n\nd) After replacement of hydraulic unit,\ncontro! unit, pulse senders or wire\nhraness as well as after work which\nmeant contact with ABS equipment\n(e.g. accident damage repairs), en-\ntlre ABS must be checked with\nBMW SERVICE TESTER.\n\n& Is Important that brake pipes and\nhoses are routed correctly.\n\ne) After each job on brake system,\nbrakes must be bled and high / low\npressure tests performed.\n\nCheck all connections for leaks.\n\nf) Brake cleaning solutions must al-\nways be kept out of brake system\nwhen cleaning brake components\nwith brake cleaners.\n\nChlorinated hydrocarbons contain-\ned In many brake cleaning products\nof various manufacturers would\nlead to corrosion of brake com-\nponents. Even most minute traces\nof brake cleaner residue must be\navoided.\n\nNote:\n\nOnly use cleaners* approved by\nBMW.\n\n* Source of Supply: HWE", "words": [["1634", 0.1924, 0.269, 0.2157, 0.2769], ["091", 0.2207, 0.2703, 0.2359, 0.2769], ["34-24", 0.4682, 0.0324, 0.5409, 0.0562], ["DESCRIPTION", 0.2732, 0.082, 0.3495, 0.0952], ["OF", 0.3535, 0.0833, 0.3687, 0.0952], ["AND", 0.3727, 0.0846, 0.396, 0.0952], ["CHECKING", 0.4, 0.0846, 0.4601, 0.0965], ["ABS", 0.4641, 0.0859, 0.4864, 0.0965], ["INDICATOR", 0.2732, 0.0991, 0.3354, 0.1124], ["LAMP", 0.3394, 0.1005, 0.3707, 0.1124], ["ABS", 0.2732, 0.1295, 0.2914, 0.152], ["Indicator", 0.2965, 0.1322, 0.3475, 0.1494], ["lamp", 0.3515, 0.1335, 0.3768, 0.1481], ["lights", 0.3808, 0.1335, 0.4101, 0.1481], ["up", 0.4141, 0.1362, 0.4273, 0.1481], ["after", 0.4303, 0.1348, 0.4551, 0.1454], ["switching", 0.2732, 0.1494, 0.3889, 0.1639], ["on", 0.3283, 0.1447, 0.3399, 0.1672], ["ignition.", 0.3439, 0.1494, 0.3889, 0.1639], ["Indicator", 0.2732, 0.1626, 0.3197, 0.1837], ["lamp", 0.3247, 0.1626, 0.348, 0.1837], ["should", 0.3545, 0.1626, 0.3884, 0.1837], ["go", 0.3949, 0.1626, 0.4061, 0.1837], ["out", 0.4111, 0.1626, 0.4288, 0.1837], ["when", 0.4338, 0.1626, 0.4571, 0.1837], ["en-", 0.4636, 0.1626, 0.4813, 0.1837], ["gine", 0.2722, 0.1791, 0.2939, 0.2009], ["has", 0.299, 0.1791, 0.3162, 